message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "rk-recall: Recall-Compensation Theorem for Runge-Kutta Error Accumulation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "rk-recall Contributors"
    email: "17319939601@163.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/selah-project/rk-recall"
url: "https://github.com/selah-project/rk-recall"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained numerical-integration module that tames Runge-Kutta error
  accumulation via a three-layer hybrid correction: (1) GamblePole discrete
  pole jump for large errors, (2) LimitCycle Poincare-Bendixson projection
  for medium errors, (3) Recall golden-ratio convex combination for small
  errors. The algorithm is decoupled from any specific ODE via an oracle
  interface (default DOP853 8th-order reference). Achieves engineering-zero
  error (epsilon < 1e-10) on harmonic oscillator; verified on Lorenz
  (chaotic, no analytical) and Van der Pol (nonlinear, no closed-form).
keywords:
  - numerical-integration
  - runge-kutta
  - error-compensation
  - dynamical-systems
  - bures-metric
  - golden-ratio
  - limit-cycle
  - dop853
  - oracle
